Z||000003||1FST2M6||03-01-2000||10:57 PM||||The record is WHAT? My car will post a best of 14.7 with the nitrous off and 95k on the clock?!?!  (13.6 with it on) here is a list of mods... <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A>  along with removing the A/C and ALL its parts, all the heat shields, the fan from the rear of the car and running on Nitto NT555R 215-60-14 @ 12 psi on Panasports S/L.   the guys that made this possible <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  What kind of rules make it "Stock"  (runs Made July 30, 1999 at Atlanta International Dragway Commerce, Ga.)<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||03-02-2000||05:15 PM||||Maybe he means stock.<P>I've also wondered what the purpose is of stripping the car down to the frame and then making a run. Seems that it's not a useful number. It's more of a number on how fast the drivetrain goes down the track since it's not really a car anymore. Might as well be R/C.<P>To me, a street car's performance should only be measured with a spare tire and jack in the trunk, full tank of gas, and two 10 year olds in the back seat. <P>Terry||||reg||1
